WEBVTT

00:00:42.150 --> 00:00:45.090
Today we are going to learn about the science of...

00:00:45.420 --> 00:00:48.280
and art in the Soviet Union.

00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:51.720
Let's see...

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:52.400
Cut!

00:00:52.580 --> 00:00:54.880
The Soviet youth is learning.

00:00:55.850 --> 00:00:56.710
In front of us...

00:00:57.480 --> 00:00:58.800
Kola the Seven-Year-Old

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:07.060
Children come here at the age of seven and study until the age of 14.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:12.860
A seven-year-old is a must for all children of the country.

00:01:16.150 --> 00:01:18.050
Strict discipline is maintained in schools.

00:01:18.070 --> 00:01:22.640
We are present at geography lessons.

00:01:25.340 --> 00:01:28.610
Children go to school six days a week.

00:01:30.090 --> 00:01:31.450
In the first four classes

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:34.700
They have four lessons a day.

00:01:35.810 --> 00:01:36.610
in the senior classes.

00:01:37.510 --> 00:01:38.330
Bon appétit!

00:01:38.980 --> 00:01:40.200
up to six lessons.

00:01:42.090 --> 00:01:44.250
When they finish this school

00:01:45.190 --> 00:01:47.290
Only a small part of the students

00:01:48.300 --> 00:01:49.960
will be able to continue his education.

00:01:51.430 --> 00:01:52.270
That's why...

00:01:52.710 --> 00:01:53.690
You need luck

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:56.580
and the best marks.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:02.010
Today...

00:02:02.300 --> 00:02:04.440
The lessons at school were over

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:07.430
The students go home.

00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:11.940
It's nice to have a rest after the lessons.

00:02:13.240 --> 00:02:15.060
Although the lessons are over...

00:02:15.670 --> 00:02:17.570
But it's too early to play.

00:02:18.390 --> 00:02:19.830
Soviet schoolchildren

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.420
There is always a lot of homework.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:26.740
And now...

00:02:27.030 --> 00:02:28.250
We are at the classes...

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:28.960
VUZI

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:38.610
A bus is a higher educational institution, a university or a special institute.

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:44.850
We are present at electrical engineering classes.

00:02:44.930 --> 00:02:49.550
We see a young teacher and a student.

00:02:49.990 --> 00:02:55.740
The main building of the Moscow State University.

00:02:57.080 --> 00:02:59.970
This building is built in comparison with the former.

00:03:00.000 --> 00:03:11.470
but the university itself was founded more than 200 years ago in 1755.

00:03:13.340 --> 00:03:20.020
Moscow State University is the largest university in the Soviet Union.

00:03:23.540 --> 00:03:28.630
About 23,000 students study at this university.

00:03:31.370 --> 00:03:32.150
And it works!

00:03:33.350 --> 00:03:35.350
more than two thousand teachers.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:39.820
Among the students there were many girls

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:41.200
and young women.

00:03:45.220 --> 00:03:45.980
A lot of women

00:03:46.950 --> 00:03:48.790
and among the teaching staff.

00:03:50.150 --> 00:03:51.550
we see a young teacher

00:03:52.970 --> 00:03:54.310
who conducts classes

00:03:55.180 --> 00:03:56.300
in a chemical laboratory.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:58.610
Only a few.

00:03:59.400 --> 00:03:59.800
...Soviet...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:01.400
young men and young women.

00:04:01.850 --> 00:04:02.910
They go to university.

00:04:04.020 --> 00:04:05.400
right after school.

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:07.680
Most of them

00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:10.160
before becoming students

00:04:11.350 --> 00:04:14.450
I have to work at factories for two years.

00:04:14.940 --> 00:04:15.780
factories...

00:04:16.090 --> 00:04:16.950
or in the farms.

00:04:18.200 --> 00:04:22.640
The main attention in the Soviet higher educational institutions

00:04:23.320 --> 00:04:25.540
is devoted to technical subjects

00:04:26.460 --> 00:04:27.520
and precise science.

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.000
The leaders of the Soviet Union...

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:36.290
of the Soviet Union strive to catch up and overtake America in economic relations.

00:04:37.400 --> 00:04:45.610
Therefore, they do not spare funds for the preparation of specialists for industry and agriculture.

00:04:47.750 --> 00:04:54.200
A lot of attention is also paid to the political education of students.

00:04:56.640 --> 00:04:59.430
Now we are in the reading room.

00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:03.440
the main library of the Moscow University.

00:05:04.140 --> 00:05:10.180
The library receives a large number of journals from abroad,

00:05:10.620 --> 00:05:17.460
but these are almost exclusively technical and scientific journals

00:05:17.670 --> 00:05:21.700
that students need for their studies.

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:28.690
The library of the Moscow University is one of the largest

00:05:28.690 --> 00:05:29.050
large

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:35.120
In the Soviet Union, a librarian publishes a technical journal.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:41.160
Here, readers can sometimes even receive the magazine America.

00:05:41.640 --> 00:05:45.460
It tells about American life.

00:05:46.400 --> 00:05:50.200
In the picture, we see the skyscrapers of New York.

00:05:51.470 --> 00:05:58.680
The magazine America is published in Washington in Russian for Soviet readers.

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:05.670
but it can be found only in a few libraries of the Soviet Union.

00:06:07.190 --> 00:06:11.790
Now we see technical and scientific journals again.

00:06:12.960 --> 00:06:16.950
Many students know foreign languages.

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:23.330
As we said, the main task of Soviet universities

00:06:23.330 --> 00:06:27.980
is to prepare technical personnel for industry.

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:38.060
Lately, nuclear energy has gained great importance.

00:06:42.490 --> 00:06:47.360
Here is the work on the Soviet nuclear power plant.

00:06:47.700 --> 00:06:59.730
The current of the power plant goes through the wires on the factory.

00:07:00.000 --> 00:07:11.150
and factories. Atomic energy is used for many purposes. In the Soviet Union, an

00:07:11.240 --> 00:07:21.740
atomic icebreaker Lenin is built, the model of which we see here. According to steel, the USSR is already

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:29.960
second in the world, but as we can see, the equipment at the factories is far from all there.

00:07:30.000 --> 00:07:39.770
And this is despite the fact that many machines are still imported from other countries.

00:07:40.280 --> 00:07:50.500
We see how metal pipes are unloaded from the ship in the Soviet port.

00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:54.000
They were brought from abroad.

00:07:54.480 --> 00:07:59.490
In the Soviet Union, domestic and foreign trade...

00:08:00.000 --> 00:08:04.590
as well as industry, is in the hands of the state.

00:08:05.790 --> 00:08:13.100
Outside the country, the state buys only what the Soviet industry and agriculture

00:08:13.100 --> 00:08:21.330
do not produce in sufficient quantity or are not able to produce at all.

00:08:22.120 --> 00:08:28.160
Most ports freeze in winter for 3-4 months.

00:08:31.690 --> 00:08:35.770
The American ship brought cargo to the Soviet port.

00:08:37.100 --> 00:08:40.080
It also helps to catch up with America.

00:08:43.720 --> 00:08:48.880
Students, as well as the Russian youth in general, love football.

00:08:49.280 --> 00:08:54.520
It is the most popular sports game in the country.

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:59.740
When there are football competitions, the tribunes of Moscow...

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:09.490
stadium Dinamo is always full. At the same stadium, physical culture parades are held annually.

00:09:09.510 --> 00:09:20.030
In three rows, like soldiers, men and women pass by the stands. In such parades

00:09:20.120 --> 00:09:28.380
gymnasts from all 15 allied republics participate. Gymnasts are well trained.

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:35.350
Each of them exactly performs its role as part of the big machine.

00:09:36.450 --> 00:09:39.550
Viewers are drawn to the grandiose spectacle.

00:09:39.970 --> 00:09:42.460
Thousands of people participate in the physical and cultural parades.

00:09:46.050 --> 00:09:54.050
Most of them are students and young workers who are engaged in sports in their free time.

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:59.970
In every university, at every factory, even in large companies,

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:03.000
There are sports clubs in the collective farms.

00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:08.480
Theatres in the Soviet Union also belong to the state.

00:10:09.120 --> 00:10:13.390
In front of us is the famous Bolshoi Theater of the USSR.

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:19.670
This is the theater of opera and ballet.

00:10:20.730 --> 00:10:23.730
Russian ballet is known all over the world.

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.540
It has great and glorious traditions.

00:10:30.350 --> 00:10:35.260
Lamps light up in the theater. The play is over.

00:10:35.640 --> 00:10:38.900
The audience liked it very much.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:48.120
The artists went to the proscenium to bow to the audience in response to her friendly applause.

00:10:48.860 --> 00:10:59.920
The circus in the Soviet Union is even more popular than the theater.

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:09.720
This is also a state institution, and all circus artists are on state service.

00:11:10.120 --> 00:11:14.700
We are present at the performance in the Moscow circus.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:18.990
The acrobat group is performing.

00:11:19.850 --> 00:11:24.020
See how skillfully and confidently they work.

00:11:24.020 --> 00:11:29.400
They work with acrobatics, compete, train.

00:11:30.000 --> 00:11:45.900
Bears, perhaps, do not have as much grace and agility in their movements as acrobats, but they also know their business very well.

00:11:46.120 --> 00:11:59.840
Neither theater nor circus can be compared to television in terms of the number of viewers. This is the most mass audience.

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:11.360
In the Soviet Union, the purpose of television is not only to entertain, but also to serve the propaganda of communist ideas.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:22.580
Now we are in one of the studios of the Moscow Television Center and we see the cameraman at work.

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:26.380
Cinema is also a mass art.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:29.440
Movies...

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:33.350
literally millions of people watch it.

00:12:34.080 --> 00:12:36.250
Therefore, in the Soviet Union,

00:12:36.430 --> 00:12:40.080
cinema is widely used for propaganda.

00:12:41.670 --> 00:12:44.580
We are present at the shooting of a film

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:48.830
from the history of the Second World War.

00:12:48.930 --> 00:12:54.110
Its purpose is to show the superiority of the Soviet army

00:12:54.110 --> 00:12:57.180
and prove to the viewer that it is invincible.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:05.400
The film industry of the Soviet Union is not concentrated in one place.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:15.290
We see how they shoot a historical picture at the Tashkent film factory in the Uzbek Soviet Republic.

00:13:16.010 --> 00:13:29.130
However, wherever the picture is shot, it, like all Soviet film industry, belongs to the state and is similar to education, science.

00:13:30.120 --> 00:13:37.270
technique and art serve the goals set by the government of the USSR.
